  "rule": "Erase all 2x2 blocks (the top-left legend row and one extra marker block), filling them with the surrounding background colour. From each single seed on the left edge, draw a path that starts moving right through the seed's region colour. It paints the legend colours cyclically, with the seed as index 0. Whenever the next cell is a wall, that wall cell gets the marker block's colour and the direction toggles between right and up. The path stops on leaving the grid, or when the cell after a turn is also a wall; that cell is not marked.",
  "scope": "Supported in random mode: grids of 16..30 per side, independent width and height. The legend has 2..4 blocks starting at column 1 on row 1 or 2, with at least two distinct colours; repeated colours are allowed. There is one marker block in a fully background 4x4 window off the legend row. Terrain is 1..3 staircase B bands rising up-right, with optional background pockets. There are 1..4 seeds, occasionally two in one band when their paths stay disjoint. Paths may end at the top or right edge or at a double wall. Fixture replay uses explicit latent terrain maps (run-length rows), pattern, marker colour and position, seed rows and legend row. Deliberately not supported: overlapping paths whose result depends on drawing order, more than two terrain colours, seeds off column 0, a missing marker block, and other path directions.",
  "constraints": [
    "Background A, path colour B, marker colour M and all pattern colours are pairwise distinct.",
    "Every 2x2 block has a fully background 3-cell-wide ring (4x4 window), so its erasure colour is unambiguous and it is an isolated 4-cell object.",
    "The marker window is disjoint from the legend zone and the marker's top row differs from the legend row, so the legend row is the unique row with the most blocks.",
    "The legend zone (rows 0..legend_row+2, columns 0..3L) is entirely background.",
    "Every terrain component (4-connected, per colour) in the input has at least 5 cells, so the only single-cell objects are the seeds and the only 2x2 objects are the blocks.",
    "Seeds sit at column 0 with B at (row,1) and are at least 2 rows apart, so they are isolated single cells under 4- and 8-connectivity.",
    "Each seed path makes at least one wall mark and has at least 4 cells, and the scene has at least 2 marks in total.",
    "Painted path cells from different seeds are disjoint. Marks only land on non-path terrain, so overlapping marks share the same colour."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Random terrain is built from monotone staircase bands plus pockets and small-component repair. It is less organic than the hand-drawn originals.",
    "Fixture replay needs the terrain map as an explicit run-length latent, because the original terrains are irregular freehand shapes.",
    "Scenes where paths would overlap are rejected rather than resolved by draw order.",
    "Generation uses bounded rejection sampling (500 attempts). It raises RuntimeError only if every attempt fails, which should be extremely rare.",
    "Assumes the reference objects() uses per-colour connected components. The constraints are written to be safe under both 4- and 8-connectivity.",
    "Explicit marker positions/seeds require explicit terrain; random mode supports requested dimensions and palette but not those positions."
  ],
